                             alt="A person walking outdoors with a Parachute pendant, knowledge graph flowing from their thoughts">
                    </picture>
                </div>
            </section>

            {# ── 1. The race we stopped chasing ── #}
            <section class="fade-up fade-up-3">
                <p class="pi-label">The race we stopped chasing</p>
                <h2 class="pi-h2">Everyone is building agents.<br>We were too. <em>We stopped.</em></h2>
                <div class="pi-prose">
                    <p>OpenAI Operator. Claude Computer Use. Manus. Devin. Perplexity. The big labs and the loudest startups are all sprinting to be <em>the</em> agent &mdash; the one that does your taxes and books your travel and answers your email.</p>
                    <p>We watched features get cloned in weeks. We watched the labs ship things our roadmap had on it, while we were still building. The labs have billions to outspend, infinite GPUs, and a head start. <strong>The agent race is a race to the bottom for everyone who isn't a lab.</strong></p>
                    <p>So we asked: what's missing? What does every agent need that none of the labs are building &mdash; because building it would weaken their lock-in?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-img">
                    {# Reused from old NVC deck slide 2: crowded agent landscape. #}
                    <picture>
                        <source type="image/webp"
                                srcset="/assets/pitch/optimized/agent-race-landscape-800w.webp 800w,
                                        /assets/pitch/optimized/agent-race-landscape-1600w.webp 1600w"
                                sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 60vw">
                        <img src="/assets/pitch/optimized/agent-race-landscape-1600w.webp"
                             alt="A crowded landscape of AI assistant icons — Operator, Cowork, Manus, Devin, Perplexity, all racing"
                             loading="lazy">
                    </picture>
                    <p class="pi-img-caption">Everyone is racing to be the agent. We're building the substrate underneath.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            {# ── 2. Voice-first ── #}
            <section class="fade-up fade-up-4">
                <p class="pi-label">The gesture that started this</p>
                <h2 class="pi-h2">It started with a voice note<br>on a walk.</h2>
                <div class="pi-prose">
                    <p>The simplest interface: <strong>press a button, talk</strong>. No app to open, no cursor, no prompt window. The thought fades fast; the gesture has to be faster.</p>
                    <p>That's where Parachute started, and it's still the front door for most people. A voice-first journal &mdash; capture as you walk, capture as you wake up, capture before the meeting starts. Local transcription by default. Audio never leaves your device unless you ask it to.</p>
                    <p>But voice was the gesture, not the product. The product is what happens to the words after they're transcribed &mdash; where they live, who can read them, what compounds over time. <strong>Voice is how Parachute meets you. Substrate is what Parachute is.</strong></p>
                </div>
            </section>

            {# ── 3. What's broken ── #}
            <section class="fade-up fade-up-5">
                <p class="pi-label">Why this is missing today</p>
                <h2 class="pi-h2">Every layer above the data<br>is fighting for the data.</h2>
                <div class="pi-prose" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <p>The tools you're using already are not on your side, and the friction shows up in the same shapes:</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-traps">
                    <div class="pi-trap">
                        <strong>Notion traps you</strong>
                        <span>Your knowledge in their database. Their AI on top. Their export rules. Switching costs grow with every doc.</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-trap">
                        <strong>Obsidian loses you</strong>
                        <span>Markdown files in folders, no AI bridge. Every tool starts cold. The power users love it; everyone else gives up.</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-trap">
                        <strong>ChatGPT forgets you</strong>
                        <span>"Memory" is a flat text file with your name and a few preferences. Every new chat starts over. You re-explain yourself for the rest of your life.</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-trap">
                        <strong>Vendor agents lock you in</strong>
                        <span>Operator runs in their cloud. Tasks live in their projects. Cowork data goes to their server. The agents are getting more powerful and your leverage is shrinking.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-prose" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <p>Parachute is the substrate underneath. Same data, different relationship: <strong>yours, on your machine, accessible to every agent and interface you choose to point at it.</strong></p>
                </div>
            </section>

            {# ── 4. The Parachute substrate ── #}
            <section class="fade-up fade-up-5">
                <p class="pi-label">The substrate</p>
                <h2 class="pi-h2">Spin up a vault.<br>Give any AI a link.</h2>
                <div class="pi-prose">
                    <p>A <strong>vault</strong> is a knowledge graph that runs on your machine. SQLite-backed. Wikilinks, full-text search, semantic search. Reachable over <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MCP</a> &mdash; the open standard every major lab now supports &mdash; and over a plain REST API. Any AI can read and write to it.</p>
                    <p>Around the vault, four small modules form the rest of the substrate:</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-img">
                    {# Reused from old NVC deck slide 5: phone/browser/pendant → Vault → Claude/ChatGPT/Gemini.
