            {# ── 6. What ships today ── #}
            <section class="fade-up fade-up-5">
                <p class="pi-label">What ships today</p>
                <h2 class="pi-h2">Five modules.<br>Installable with one command.</h2>
                <div class="pi-prose">
                    <p><code>parachute install &lt;module&gt;</code>. The hub coordinates lifecycle, OAuth, and the service catalog. We launched the first version on <strong>April 23, 2026</strong>; everything below is live.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-modules">
                    <div class="pi-mod">
                        <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                        <h3>Vault</h3>
                        <p>SQLite-backed graph. REST + MCP. Wikilinks, full-text and semantic search, Obsidian import/export.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-mod">
                        <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                        <h3>Scribe</h3>
                        <p>Whisper-compatible transcription API. Local by default; BYO cloud provider.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-mod">
                        <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                        <h3>Notes</h3>
                        <p>Browser-based companion for the Vault. Installable PWA, works offline, voice capture wired to Scribe.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-mod">
                        <span class="pi-mod-tag">Core</span>
                        <h3>Hub</h3>
                        <p>The coordinator. Install, start, stop, expose. OAuth issuer with scope-narrowed JWTs and per-module admin UIs.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-mod">
                        <span class="pi-mod-tag exploration">Exploration</span>
                        <h3>Paraclaw</h3>
                        <p>A Parachute distribution &mdash; a fork of NanoClaw with vault integration, exploring an opinionated all-in-one.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-mod">
                        <span class="pi-mod-tag">Patterns</span>
                        <h3>Module protocol</h3>
                        <p><code>info</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>services.json</code>, <code>well-known</code>. The contract third-party modules plug into.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            {# ── 7. Cloud ── #}
            <section class="fade-up fade-up-5">
                <p class="pi-label">The convenience path</p>
                <h2 class="pi-h2">Self-host or let us host.<br>Same code. Same exits.</h2>
                <div class="pi-prose">
                    <p>Most people don't want to run a server. <strong>Parachute Cloud</strong> is the same modules, managed for you &mdash; vault, transcription, multi-device sync, public exposure done correctly. You bring your AI client. We run the substrate.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-tiers">
                    <div class="pi-tier">
                        <div class="pi-tier-price">Free<span>&nbsp;</span></div>
                        <div class="pi-tier-body"><strong>Self-host</strong> &mdash; all modules, AGPL, run anywhere</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-tier featured">
                        <div class="pi-tier-price">~$5<span>/mo</span></div>
                        <div class="pi-tier-body"><strong>Cloud</strong> &mdash; managed vault + transcription, multi-device sync, OAuth-gated public exposure</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-tier">
                        <div class="pi-tier-price">Custom<span>&nbsp;</span></div>
                        <div class="pi-tier-body"><strong>Org / pro</strong> &mdash; team vaults, private deployments, extended modules</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="pi-prose" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
                    <p>Same shape as self-hosted. Export everything. Leave at any time. <strong>The cloud is a convenience, not a SaaS ladder.</strong> We're not pricing your context.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

